# The Dockerfile installs dependencies and *then* copies the source, so
# anything left here that shares a name with something the image already built
# lands on top of it. A node_modules built on the developer's machine would
# replace the one installed for the image's own platform — for a package that
# drives Chromium, that is a container that builds cleanly and then fails at
# runtime for no visible reason.
node_modules

# Auth data and downloaded media. These are a mounted volume at runtime; baking
# a copy of someone's linked session into an image is both wrong and unsafe.
data

# Secrets belong in the environment, not in a layer. compose passes them with
# env_file, so the image never needs its own copy.
.env

.git
.gitignore
npm-debug.log*
